-- title:
--   Level automorphisms are compatible with q ↦ q^ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ be primes with $\ell \ne q$, let $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $\iota_0 : L \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfies $\iota_0(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Write $H_n = \ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/n^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/n)^{\times}\bigr)$, as given by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), and let $K$, resp. $K_q$, be the intermediate field of $L(\!(T)\!)$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_{q\ell}}((q\ell)^2M')$, resp. of $\Gamma_{H_q}(q^2M')$, under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Fix $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $L$-algebra automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ and $\tau_q$ of $K_q$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ at level $q\ell$ read through $\xi$, resp. at level $q$ read through $\xi^{\ell}$: that is, for all $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all weight-$k$ forms $f,g$ on the relevant group whose $q$-expansions come from integral power series $p_f,p_g$ with $p_g \ne 0$ as a Laurent series, all $x$ in the field whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and all $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending the designated root of unity to $e^{2\pi i/n}$ ($n = q\ell$, resp. $q$), one has $\iota(\tau x) \cdot \mathrm{qExp}(g \mid_k \mathrm{diag}(n,1)^{-1}\gamma^{-1}\mathrm{diag}(n,1)) = \mathrm{qExp}(f \mid_k \mathrm{diag}(n,1)^{-1}\gamma^{-1}\mathrm{diag}(n,1))$. Then for $x \in K_q$ and $w \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is obtained from that of $x$ by the substitution $T \mapsto T^{\ell}$ (the exponent-scaling ring homomorphism [`ModularCurve.qExpand`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25)), the expansion of $\tau w$ is obtained from that of $\tau_q x$ by the same substitution.
--
--   This is the restriction-of-level compatibility of the level automorphisms of the full-level modular function fields: passing from level $q$ to level $q\ell$ along $z \mapsto \ell z$ intertwines the automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ at the two levels. It is used in the description of the Galois action on the $q$-expansions of the full-level functions, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_isLevelAutAt_apply_eq_iff_exists_eq_qExpand_gamma0_of_exists_ringHom`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_isLevelAutAt_apply_eq_iff_exists_eq_qExpand_gamma0_of_exists_ringHom) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAut_apply_qExpand_jq_eq_jqNModC_of_antidiagonal_of_ringHom`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAut_apply_qExpand_jq_eq_jqNModC_of_antidiagonal_of_ringHom).
